Market Restraints: Costs, Competition, and Implementation Challenges
Catheter-Related Complications
Central venous hemodialysis catheters carry risks including infection, thrombosis, and catheter dysfunction.
Preference for Permanent Vascular Access
Arteriovenous fistulas and grafts may be preferred for suitable patients requiring ongoing dialysis, limiting the appropriate use of catheters.
Regulatory and Quality Requirements
Manufacturers must satisfy applicable medical device requirements and maintain validated sterile production processes.
Procurement Budget Constraints
Dialysis centers and healthcare facilities must balance product quality, clinical requirements, and treatment costs.
Supply Chain Reliability
Catheter shortages or product recalls can disrupt healthcare procurement and treatment planning.
